        "raw": "<p>Ronway&#39;s questions, answer number 1!</p><p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/answers-to-debated-questions-3871\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/answers-to-debated-questions-3871</a></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family: 'PT Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><strong>1. Do you choose a target while using Jack Handle?</strong></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px; color: rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family: 'PT Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">No, it is an automatic effect, so you will read strike as &quot;do all non-hero targets 1 melee damage&quot; or any other damage he can do pretty much. So targeting Fixer when he has Bloody Knuckles doesn&#39;t cause Fixer to deal out 5 melee damage to all non-hero targets.</p>",
